# Frontend rules - HITSHCM

- Prefer Next.js App Router patterns already in the repo.
- Use TypeScript strict styles; avoid `any` unless justified in a comment.
- Tailwind for styling; reuse existing tokens/patterns before inventing new ones.
- Keep components focused; extract only when reuse is real.
- Handle loading, empty, and error states for user-facing flows.
- Accessibility: semantic HTML, labels on inputs, keyboard-reachable actions.
- Do not fetch privileged data in client components without an approved pattern.
